Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 11:54:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 010/143] dts: opi4a: the framebuffer reclaims the DE and VO0
 power domains of pck600

When loading panfrost as a module, ALL consumers of pck600 get probed and
its sync_state() powers off the domains with no consumer: DE and VO0 die ->
the U-Boot FB scanout stops and the screen goes black mid-boot (confirmed
live: DE/VO0 'off-0' in pm_genpd_summary after modprobe panfrost; until now
they survived only because without modules the GPU never probed and
sync_state stayed pending forever). The simple-framebuffer binding accepts
power-domains and simpledrm manages them (multi-domain via genpd).
---
 .../boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts    | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
index dbac7419f..2afd4cfed 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
@@ -45,6 +45,17 @@ framebuffer@bbea2000 {
 			height = <768>;
 			stride = <5440>;
 			format = "x8r8g8b8";
+			/*
+			 * Claim the display pipeline power domains that U-Boot left
+			 * powered on. Without this, as soon as ALL the
+			 * pck600 consumers have probed (e.g. panfrost as a
+			 * module), its sync_state() sweeps the domains with no
+			 * consumer and powers DE and VO0 off -> black screen half-way
+			 * through boot (seen live 2026-07-08: DE/VO0 off-0 in
+			 * pm_genpd_summary tras modprobe panfrost). simpledrm
+			 * supports multiple power-domains and keeps them on.
+			 */
+			power-domains = <&pck600 PD_DE>, <&pck600 PD_VO0>;
 		};
 	};
 
